# Links the link checker cannot reach from a GitHub runner, with the reason each one is here.
#
# An exclusion hides a rotted citation as effectively as it hides a firewall, so nothing goes in
# this file on a hunch. Each line below was measured: the check was run once without this file at
# all, and these are the ones that failed, with the error the runner actually reported. Every one
# of them answers 200 from a browser in Türkiye, so the failure is the runner's path to the host,
# not a dead source.
#
# Re-measure before adding a line, and delete a line when the host starts answering. The run that
# produced the current list: actions/runs/35665251647.

# TLS handshake fails from the runner — the TRNC gazette's certificate chain is not accepted
# there. The documents themselves are live and are the official coordinates behind the licence
# blocks (ADR 0015).
^https://basimevi\.gov\.ct\.tr/AR%C5%9E%C4%B0V/2011$
^https://basimevi\.gov\.ct\.tr/Portals/6/2011/161\.pdf$
^https://basimevi\.gov\.ct\.tr/Portals/6/2011/198\.pdf$
^https://basimevi\.gov\.ct\.tr/Portals/6/2017/182\.pdf$
^https://basimevi\.gov\.ct\.tr/Portals/6/2023/219\.pdf$

# Connection reset by peer from the runner.
^https://www\.mgk\.gov\.tr/index\.php/29-mart-2017-tarihli-toplanti$

# A SPARQL endpoint, not a page: it answers 403 to a bare GET by design. It is cited as the
# interface a query was run against, and there is nothing for a link checker to fetch.
^https://query\.wikidata\.org/sparql$
